 ## Background
-The framework originated from the need to reconstruct high-quality volumes from noisy and angle-limited tilt-series in cryogenic electron tomography (Cryo-ET) [S1]. It was formalized as a proximal algorithm framework to handle non-smooth, constrained, and large-scale optimization problems [S1]. The approach was subsequently generalized to X-ray CT for 3D super-resolution, sparse view reconstruction, and space-time reconstruction of deforming objects [S2, unofficial]. It has also been applied to dynamic fluid capture using RGB cameras [S2, unofficial] and generative reconstruction using deep learning priors [S3, unofficial].
